\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0   Just as I am, without one plea
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 But that your blood was shed for me,
\par And that you call us, 'Come to me',
\par O Lamb of God, I come.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.   Just as I am, though tossed about
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 With many a conflict, many a doubt,
\par Fightings and fears within, without,
\par O Lamb of God, I come.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.   Just as I am you will receive,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Will welcome, pardon, cleanse, relieve;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Because your promise I believe,
\par O Lamb of God, I come.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.   Just as I am - your love unknown
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Has broken every barrier down -
\par Now to be yours, and yours alone,
\par O Lamb of God, I come.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.   Just as I am, of that free love
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj The breadth, length, depth, and
\par height to prove,
\par Here for a season, then above -
\par \pard     O Lamb of God, I come.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

